<BES xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="BES.xsd">
  <Analysis>
    <Title>Pre Cache Relevant Fixlets</Title>
    <Description><![CDATA[Generates a space delimited result of all relevant fixlet IDs that can be copied/pasted directly into the BES Support "File Pre-Cache Wizard." This will allow you to send all of the sha files to a specific endpoint that are relevant to that endpoint without having to start the patching/fixlet process. This fixlet is specific to a custom site, just change the name of the site to whatever you choose, i.e. "Patches for Windows (English)" if you want to use the Tivoli site.&nbsp;

*I also filter out certain fixlets as "Internal", just remove that clause if you use "Internal" fixlets.]]></Description>
    <Relevance>true</Relevance>
    <MIMEField>
      <Name>x-fixlet-modification-time</Name>
      <Value>Tue, 04 Jun 2013 12:55:40 +0000</Value>
    </MIMEField>
    <Domain>BESC</Domain>
    <Property ID="1" Name="IDs">concatenations &quot; &quot; of (ids of relevant fixlets whose (not exists values of headers &quot;X-Fixlet-Type&quot; of it or (value of headers &quot;X-Fixlet-Type&quot; of it as lowercase != &quot;task&quot; and value of headers &quot;X-Fixlet-Type&quot; of it as lowercase != &quot;analysis&quot; and value of headers &quot;X-Fixlet-Source&quot; of it != &quot;Internal&quot;)) of sites whose (name of it = &quot;My Custom Site&quot;) as string)</Property>
  </Analysis>
</BES>
